(6938406, 1044846, 135697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kgeary:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you all for the kind words. To answer Ryan''s question, the lights are a combination of net lights and string lights. Here''s a BTS shot:<br/> <br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ve seen how this technique is done a few times elsewhere and it is very effective, and you expertly used it here for a great photo and yes a wonderful christmas card, simple and elegant, but doesnt take away from those who used the whole family or themselves as per the challenge, congratulations nonetheless :O) and truly Merry Christmas :O)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-12-20 19:46:40.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kgeary: Thank you all for the kind words. To answer Ryan''s question, the lights are a combination of net lights and string lights. Here''s a BTS shot:   I''ve seen how this technique is done a few times elsewhere and it is very effective, and you expertly used it here for a great photo and yes a wonderful christmas card, simple and elegant, but doesnt take away from those who used the whole family or themselves as per the challenge, congratulations nonetheless :O) and truly Merry Christmas :O)', '2012-12-20 19:34:25.000000', '2012-12-20 19:46:40.000000', 0),
